    title: "Keeping the household fire",
    text: "A Vedic householder kindled his own fire at marriage and was meant to keep it alive till death. Morning and evening he, or a priest for him, poured milk or ghee into it, the agnihotra, with a verse to Agni and Surya. Grander rites, the shrauta sacrifices with three fires, soma pressing and animal offerings, needed teams of priests and were for the rich and royal. The domestic rites of the Grihya Sutras were for everyone of the upper varnas: offerings of cooked food scattered for the gods, the ancestors, the animals and the house spirits, before anyone ate. Women tended the fire in practice; the ritual texts give the wife a fixed seat beside her husband.",
