    evidence: "documented",
    title: "Learning the Veda by ear",
    text: "At the upanayana, the thread ceremony, a boy of the upper varnas was handed to a teacher and began brahmacharya, a student's life of begging food, tending the teacher's fire and memorising. The Veda was never learned from writing. The teacher recited, the pupil repeated, word by word and then in woven patterns, pairs and reversals, so that no syllable or pitch accent could drift. It could take twelve years for one Veda. This worked: the Rigveda has come down with almost no variation for three thousand years. Girls, save a few in the early period, and all the lower orders, learned their skills at home from parents, as nearly everyone did.",
