    text: "A stone inscription at Mandsaur, dated to 436 CE with an addition of 473, is the story of a guild. Silk weavers from Lata, southern Gujarat, drawn by the fame of the king, migrated to Dashapura and prospered. Some kept weaving; others, the poem says, became archers, astrologers, storytellers and ascetics, yet the guild held together and paid for a temple to the sun, then repaired it when it decayed. It praises their silk cloth as finer than a woman's youth and adornment. It shows a craft group moving as a body, changing jobs but keeping its identity: something close to what later became a jati.",
