    text: "The physician, vaidya, learned from a teacher, and the Charaka Samhita tells the student to swear to devote himself to the sick, not to betray patients' secrets and not to treat the king's enemies. Ayurveda explained illness as imbalance among three doshas, wind, bile and phlegm, corrected by diet, oils, purges, sweating and compound drugs from roots, barks, minerals and ghee. The Sushruta Samhita describes surgery: lancing, suturing with ant heads as clips, couching cataracts, and rebuilding a cut-off nose with a flap of cheek skin, noses being a common punishment. Most people saw a vaidya rarely; they were treated at home by older women, and by village healers who used mantras as much as herbs.",
