    title: "The first stone temples and puja",
    text: "In the Gupta centuries worship moved from the sacrificial fire to the image. Small stone shrines like Deogarh and the cave shrines at Udayagiri housed Vishnu, Shiva and the Goddess, and worship was puja: the deity was woken, bathed, dressed, offered flowers, lamps, incense and food, and then seen, darshan, by worshippers who came to look and be looked at. The Puranas, the great story collections, were composed and recited in this age, and gave each god a mythology that ordinary people could hear at festivals. Puja needed no Vedic learning from the worshipper, which is part of why it spread; a household could do it at home with a clay image and a lamp.",
